From: yogesh1239 <77014257+yogesh1239@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 17:37:49 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Patches: fix sprint dropping to half speed at high frame
 rates

The wall detector in the movement update (0x1914500) treats the character
as blocked when the distance moved in one frame * 30.0 is below 1.0. That
threshold was written for 30 FPS: above ~147 FPS the sprint ramp falls
under it, the slowdown scale decays x0.8 to 0.5 and locks sprint at half
speed. Divide by the frame dt ([rbp-0x74]) instead, so the test is
"speed below 1 unit/s" at every frame rate (the original 30 FPS rule).

Added to "Uncap FPS++" and "90 FPS++". Tested live: sprint 6.7-6.95 u/s
at 60/120/200/240 FPS targets (was ~3.2 at 200/240); run speed unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Vb32d7skPfMztipqAdXvPt
